    <h3>Questions 1–6</h3>
    <p class="instr">Complete the notes below.<br>
    Choose <b>ONE WORD ONLY</b> from the passage for each answer.</p>

    <div>
      <div>Dolls</div>
      
      <div>Earliest known dolls</div>
      <div>• represented religious figures</div>
      <div>• used as toys</div>

      <div>Egypt 2000 BC</div>
      <div>• bodies were made of wood</div>
      <div>• <span class="ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">1</strong><input type="text" class="q-input" name="practice_single_reading_50_1" id="practice_single_reading_50_1_" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 1" placeholder="Answer"></span> was used for the hair</div>

      <div>Ancient Greece and Rome</div>
      <div>• dolls were given to <span class="ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">2</strong><input type="text" class="q-input" name="practice_single_reading_50_2" id="practice_single_reading_50_2_" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 2" placeholder="Answer"></span> by older girls</div>

      <div>600 BC</div>
      <div>• realistic dolls had separate clothes and <span class="ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">3</strong><input type="text" class="q-input" name="practice_single_reading_50_3" id="practice_single_reading_50_3_" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 3" placeholder="Answer"></span> that could be put in different positions</div>

      <div>17th and 18th centuries</div>
      <div>• dolls made of <span class="ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">4</strong><input type="text" class="q-input" name="practice_single_reading_50_4" id="practice_single_reading_50_4_" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 4" placeholder="Answer"></span> became more common</div>
      <div>• moulds made of <span class="ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">5</strong><input type="text" class="q-input" name="practice_single_reading_50_5" id="practice_single_reading_50_5_" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 5" placeholder="Answer"></span></div>

      <div>1800s</div>
      <div>• new manufacturing process developed</div>
      <div>• new group of mixtures known as <span class="ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">6</strong><input type="text" class="q-input" name="practice_single_reading_50_6" id="practice_single_reading_50_6_" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 6" placeholder="Answer"></span></div>
      <div>• recipes for these mixtures kept secret</div>
    </div>

    
    <h3>Questions 7–13</h3>
